# AI Board NAT Controller — SNAT configuration v0.3.0
# Enabled|Source|Destination|Protocol|DestinationPort|TranslateTo
#
# Enabled: 1 (enabled), 0 (disabled; still syntax-checked).
# Source: IPv4 or CIDR (192.168.1.100, 192.168.1.0/24,
#         0.0.0.0/0 for all sources). Network-aligned CIDRs required.
# Destination: any, IPv4, or network-aligned CIDR.
# Protocol: any, tcp, udp, icmp (case-sensitive).
# DestinationPort: any, 443, or inclusive range 8000:9000.
#                  TCP/UDP only; use any for other protocols.
#                  Valid numbers 1–65535; no leading zeroes.
# TranslateTo: WAN_IP (validated primary address) or explicit IPv4
#              assigned/routed by your ISP; ownership not validated.
# IPv4 octets and prefixes must be decimal without leading zeroes.
# Rules evaluated in file order; first matching SNAT wins.
# Unmatched traffic falls through to ASUS rules. WAN interface automatic.
# Empty ruleset installs an empty managed chain in ENFORCE.
# All six fields mandatory, no spaces or inline comments.
# Blank lines and full-line # comments ignored.
# Invalid input blocks entire update; existing NAT stays in place.
# Existing connections may retain previous mappings.
# Replace atomically using sibling .new file and mv.
#
# Examples (inactive; replace documentation addresses locally):
# 1|192.168.1.100|198.51.100.20|tcp|443|WAN_IP
# 1|192.168.1.0/24|any|tcp|8000:9000|WAN_IP
# 1|192.168.1.100/32|any|any|any|203.0.113.11
# 0|192.168.1.100|any|udp|53|WAN_IP
#
# Active configuration — intentionally disabled example:
0|192.168.1.100|198.51.100.20|tcp|443|WAN_IP
